#3902
The Twisty Part Of The River~
   The Widmans River twists and turns here as the Uller River pours into
it from the north, and the meeting of the two currents nearly tosses you
out of your boat.  The water is dark and cold, with an almost reptilian
sheen, and it seems almost alive.  The current runs east, but you could
probably fight hard enough to row north up the Uller, or west
downstream.
