#3911
The North Channel~
   The river splits as it runs up against the northern tip of the
island, the water churning white where it breaks against the rocks.  A
navigable channel slips off to the west between the island and the steep
riverbank, while the main current sweeps on towards the delta to the
south.  Willows lean out over the water, trailing their branches in the
current.
