#3912
The North Channel~
   The river current carries you swiftly westward as the channel begins
to narrow, squeezing past the north end of the island.  On your left the
island's banks are thick with reeds and tall grass; on your right the
far shore rises in a wall of gray rock.  The water here is deep and
dark, and you must work to keep your boat from turning in the eddies.
